  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows Hospira, Inc. discontinued manufacture of diltiazem hydrochloride injection on 2026-01-05; the shortage has been posted for 104 months as of 2026-10-21",
  "headline_cites": ["E24", "D14"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list records that Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, discontinued manufacture of diltiazem hydrochloride injection with an initial posting date of 2026-01-05.",
      "cites": ["E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 104 months.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label for NDC 00409435003 names Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1925262) as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 976095 at that plant ended 2016-06-08 and was classified OAI, 623 days before the 2018-02-21 shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E11", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2017-02-14, 372 days before the 2018-02-21 posting.",
      "cites": ["E16", "D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1064827 at the plant ended 2018-08-15 and was classified OAI, 175 days after the 2018-02-21 posting.",
      "cites": ["E13", "D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based best option is to buy from HF Acquisition Co LLC, DBA HealthFirst, which is not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    }
  ]
}
